From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:05:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: panorama masonry appends pages without a full
 relayout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each paging page builds a new items lambda. The layout epoch mixed the
shape-table version with that lambda's identity, so the cache could not
append: every page, and every loading-footer add or remove, rebuilt the
whole shelf. That structural relayout was 16-20 ms mid-fling, and frames
dropped to 53-62% of animation ticks while new covers loaded.

The high 32 bits stay the shape table. A longer list with those bits
unchanged appends when the keys already laid out still match, even if
the lambda is a new instance. One changed key at the old end, the
loading footer swapping for the next page, is placed again and the cells
above it stay. A change before that prefix rebuilds. The same count with
a new lambda still rebuilds, so a lambda on every coast frame keeps
eating the fling.

与 anikku-harmony 0030 同一段代码，Anikku 侧待移植。
